[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The link between a node and its code is prose in both directions, and unchecked in both

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[EVIDENCE]
UID: MECH-NODE-CODE-LINKAGE-IS-PROSE
TITLE: The link between a node and its code is prose in both directions, and unchecked in both
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
TWO READINGS, both kept, because the later one is what this node was filed to
provoke.

AS MEASURED 2026-08-27. Nothing joined a node to the code it describes.
Outward, three File relations existed in the whole 144-node graph, on two
nodes, all naming implementation files -- `packages/semble/lib/withGrammars.nix`
twice and `packages/semble/patches/extra-grammars.patch` -- against 15 nodes at
implemented and 3 at verified. `SLICE-GRAPH-CHECKS` was verified and
`checks/strictdoc-cycle-check.nix` existed for it with no edge between them;
`SLICE-GRAMMAR-FROM-NIX` was implemented against five flake checks and a
package directory with no edge to any of them. So the claim that code landed
was prose in NOTES, and the query `DEPTH == implemented` could not be joined to
what it implemented. Inward, measured over the git-tracked non-.sdoc tree: 67
UID citations in 34 files, 61 of them naming a node under `docs/plans/` and 27
distinct plan nodes cited, plus two tokens that resolved to nothing at all --
`MECH-SAMPLE` and `SLICE-UID`. Two mechanisms were wanted and they shared one
input: require a File edge to the implementing file or check at implemented,
and lint the source-comment citations against the same UID-to-file map
`MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK` builds.

AS OF 2026-09-03. The outward half is mostly closed and the inward half has a
carrier. The corpus carries 64 File relations on 37 nodes, 4 of them
element-grained -- an ELEMENT and ID naming one item of a file rather than the
whole of it -- and none using a LINE_RANGE. Source traceability is on, so
strictdoc resolves those relations itself at parse time, and
`dev/scripts/element-check.py` gates the element-grained ones as
strictdoc-element-check in nix flake check. Inward, a source comment can now
carry a real edge rather than a citation: `@relation(UID, scope=function)`
written as the FIRST line of a comment block links code to a node, in any file
a configured glob claims. One such marker exists, in devenv.nix, naming
EV-STRICTDOC-EXPORT-TIMING.

WHAT IS STILL OPEN is exactly the pair of mechanisms named above. Nothing
requires a File edge of a node at implemented, so the join remains a
convention. And the 67 prose citations are still prose: an extractor reads
`@relation()` markers, not a bare UID in a sentence, so no lint over them
exists and none of them became an edge.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The inward half was expected to arm on a date nobody chooses, and that
prediction was wrong in a way worth recording. It read: none of the 67 is an
edge today, so none can dangle; all 61 plan-node citations become inbound
violations of `INV-NO-EXTERNAL-PLAN-REFS` on the day a source-comment
extractor exists, which is `DEC-ARCH-COLOCATION`'s retirement condition. The
extractor landed on 2026-09-02 and none of them became anything. An extractor
reads `@relation()` markers with a Lark grammar; a bare UID in prose is not a
marker and is not parsed. So the citations are inert by shape rather than by
timing, and the lint that would check them is still unbuilt and still wanted.

The outward half is what makes the requirement worth stating at all: a File
relation whose VALUE names a path that does not exist used to export with exit
0 (`MECH-FILE-RELATION-EXISTENCE`), so requiring the edge meant nothing without
that check beside it. That gap is closed twice over now -- by the corpus
checker and by upstream's own validation -- which leaves the requirement itself
as the only missing piece.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Measured 2026-08-27. `MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK` puts the source-annotation arm explicitly out of scope with a reason — strictdoc_config.py sets no source root and `@relation` comments never reach the JSON export — so this is unowned rather than deferred. `MECH-TESTS-AS-CONTRACT` scopes its verified requirement to flows deliberately, noting that the same rule applied to every node would invalidate both then-verified nodes on the day it landed; the same corpus-first order applies here. Not decided here: whether the 61 existing citations are remediated or grandfathered until the extractor lands.

Absorbs the proposed `MECH-ANNOTATION-TARGET-DURABILITY` and `MECH-NODE-TO-CODE-EDGE-COVERAGE`.

Retyped from MECHANISM to EVIDENCE on 2026-08-30 by the mechanism mood test under DEC-NODE-FAMILIES, with medium confidence after a second opinion: it records what was observed once, not how something always behaves. Noted for a later split: The closing sentence names two mechanisms wanted, one of them a requirement to be written: 'require a File edge to the implementing file or check at implemented', plus a lint of source-comment citations against the UID-to-file map. The UID keeps its prefix: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE.
Updated 2026-09-03 for commits 0496adfe, c64a0147, 7d6886d1 and 62a1be71.
`MECH-PLAN-REFS-CHECK`'s note that the source-annotation arm is out of scope
because strictdoc_config.py sets no source root is stale on its premise: the
config now sets source_root_path and turns REQUIREMENT_TO_SOURCE_TRACEABILITY
on, and an `@relation` comment in a file a glob claims does reach the export.
The arm is still unowned, but it is no longer unreachable.
<<<
